<title>INDIA: India's 96/97 rice procurement seen at 11.5 mln T.</title>
<headline>India's 96/97 rice procurement seen at 11.5 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian government agencies are expected to procure around 11.5 million tonnes of rice in 1996/97 (October-September) against 9.9 million tonnes last year, Food Minister Devendra Prasad Yadav said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are expecting that the total  procurement of rice for the central pool in 1996/97 will be around 11.5 million tonnes as against 9.9 million in the year 1995/96,&quot; Yadav told a meeting of state food ministers.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
